{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Joseph could not refrain himself before all those who stood by him.</b> It appears from this that those who stood by him who were there in the royal palace were softening toward him on this account, because their hearts were moved by the entreaties of Judah. And Scripture tells that Joseph could not bear this and strengthen his heart against them all, and on this account he called, <b>'Cause every man to go out from me'</b>, and afterward <b>he gave forth his voice in weeping</b> — that is, when they had gone out — <b>and the Egyptians heard, and the house of Pharaoh heard.</b>" "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'And Joseph could not refrain himself' — Rabbi Samuel bar Nahmani said: Joseph brought his soul into great distress at that hour, for if they had killed him, no creature could have saved him and no creature would call him to account. And why did he say, 'Cause every man to go out from me'? He said: It is better that I be killed than that I shame their faces in public."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:17.455042053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}